{"signature": "{\"text\": \"Here is a GCSE-style question worth three marks. Explain how cavity wall insulation reduces the rate of energy transfer from a heated house. A model answer is: insulating foam has a low thermal conductivity, so energy passes through it relatively slowly by conduction. It also traps air in small pockets, reducing conduction and preventing large convection currents within the cavity. Consequently, less energy is transferred from the warm interior to the colder exterior each second. Award one mark for low thermal conductivity, one for the role of trapped air or reduced convection, and one for the reduced rate of energy transfer.\", \"voice\": \"en-NG-AbeoNeural\", \"rate\": \"-4%\", \"eleven\": true}", "duration": 48.666122, "words": [["Here", 0.0], ["is", 0.441], ["a", 0.731], ["GCSE-style", 0.917], ["question", 2.461], ["worth", 2.995], ["three", 3.344], ["marks.", 3.657], ["Explain", 4.272], ["how", 4.981], ["cavity", 5.329], ["wall", 5.828], ["insulation", 6.235], ["reduces", 7.036], ["the", 7.709], ["rate", 7.872], ["of", 8.115], ["energy", 8.29], ["transfer", 8.766], ["from", 9.567], ["a", 10.031], ["heated", 10.252], ["house.", 10.739], ["A", 11.482], ["model", 11.749], ["answer", 12.225], ["is:", 12.759], ["insulating", 13.201], ["foam", 13.932], ["has", 14.373], ["a", 14.675], ["low", 14.826], ["thermal", 15.116], ["conductivity,", 15.639], ["so", 16.765], ["energy", 17.067], ["passes", 17.624], ["through", 18.135], ["it", 18.483], ["relatively", 18.773], ["slowly", 19.47], ["by", 20.201], ["conduction.", 20.526], ["It", 21.56], ["also", 21.815], ["traps", 22.21], ["air", 22.779], ["in", 23.255], ["small", 23.499], ["pockets,", 23.928], ["reducing", 24.857], ["conduction", 25.472], ["and", 26.157], ["preventing", 26.389], ["large", 27.098], ["convection", 27.504], ["currents", 28.235], ["within", 28.862], ["the", 29.408], ["cavity.", 29.582], ["Consequently,", 30.557], ["less", 31.625], ["energy", 31.974], ["is", 32.461], ["transfer